What is Cyber Insurance?
Cyber insurance is a specialized insurance product designed to protect businesses and individual users from a wide array of internet-based risks. This coverage typically encompasses first-party protection for direct losses from events like data destruction, extortion, theft, hacking, and denial-of-service attacks. It also provides essential third-party liability coverage for losses incurred by others due to errors and omissions, failure to safeguard sensitive data, or defamation. Modern policies often extend beyond financial indemnification to include invaluable benefits such as proactive security audits, expert post-incident public relations support, comprehensive investigative expenses, and even criminal reward funds to aid in recovery.
